You are coordinating a smart farm and must manage a drone fleet that protects crops from birds. The main objective is to minimize crop damage across every field.

At the start, birds move around the farm randomly. At times they decide to feed, choose a target field, and fly toward it. Their preference over fields changes over time, and they are also more attracted to fields where more birds are already present. After a bird lands in a field, it waits for a fixed period before causing damage. Once damage is dealt, the bird either attacks another crop in the same field or leaves the area.

Every field has sensors that detect bird presence. A field with more birds reports a higher threat level.

A drone can be assigned to a target field; it then travels there and hovers above it. Because drone speed is 2, protection starts only after travel time. The drone scares birds within a certain radius, but fully protecting a field requires multiple drones. Scared birds may relocate within the same field and continue feeding. Only when a field is fully protected do birds flee away, so partial protection is not very effective, though still better than no protection.

Your task is to distribute drones among fields to reduce bird-caused damage as much as possible. You will repeatedly receive the current state (drone positions, threat levels, and similar information) and must assign drones to fields.



